# 002 · CI on every push, and repository settings

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Tester basics

## What

Run CI on every push to the development branch, not only on pull requests and `main`. Set up the GitHub repository for outside people: a ruleset on `main`, private vulnerability reporting, Dependabot, and correct topics.

## Why

The code moves to `main` only as the last step of the release. Without this change, CI would run for the first time at the very end.

## Done when

- [x] CI runs on every push to the development branch and passes there.
- [ ] `main` accepts changes only through pull requests that pass CI.
- [ ] Private vulnerability reporting and Dependabot are on.
- [ ] The repository's topics are spelled correctly.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: Yes to the repository settings, as part of v0.1.0.
- 2026-10-21, owner: The ruleset's bypass list gets the **Repository admin** role, with **Always allow**. When the release pull request's checks pass, its commit is pushed to `main`, so the commits keep their IDs.

## Open questions

- The repository settings need the owner's GitHub account. The checklist in Progress says what to set.
- Answered 2026-10-21 (see Decisions): the release reaches `main` through the admin bypass.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-20: CI (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) now runs on every push to `v1/build`, as well as on pull requests and pushes to `main`. A new commit on a pull request cancels the older run. Every push to `main` or `v1/build` gets a whole run of its own. The contributing page says what CI runs. The first box waits for a push to `v1/build` that shows every job green.
- 2026-10-20: `.github/dependabot.yml` asks for weekly updates: npm at the root and in `docs/_site`, and GitHub Actions. Minor and patch updates come grouped. Starlight updates come alone, because Starlight is still 0.x. Dependabot reads this file only from the default branch, so the version updates start when the code reaches `main`. Since 2026-10-20, when the code moved to `main` early, the file sends them to `v1/build`, where work goes on.
- 2026-10-20: The owner's steps, in the repository's settings on GitHub. Nothing in the repository changes them:
  - [ ] **Ruleset on `main`:** Settings › Rules › Rulesets › New ruleset › New branch ruleset. Name: `main`. Enforcement status: **Active**. Target branches: **Include default branch**. Rules: **Restrict deletions**; **Block force pushes**; **Require a pull request before merging**, with 0 required approvals; **Require status checks to pass**, with **Require branches to be up to date before merging** and these checks: `checks (Node 22)`, `checks (Node 24)`, `docs site`, `secret scan`, `compose-smoke`. Bypass list: **Repository admin**, **Always allow** (see Decisions).
  - [ ] **Private vulnerability reporting:** Settings › Advanced Security › Private vulnerability reporting › **Enable**.
  - [ ] **Dependabot alerts:** Settings › Advanced Security › Dependabot alerts › **Enable**.
  - [ ] **Topics:** the repository's main page › **About** (the gear icon) › **Topics**. Remove `harnes`, which is misspelled; `harness` is already there. The topics after: `agent-tools`, `artificial-intelligence`, `auto-research`, `autonomous-agents`, `harness`, `harness-framework`, `llm`.
- 2026-10-20: CI run 39479049337 on `v1/build` (85b4de0) passed every job: both checks, the docs site, the secret scan, the compose smoke, the quick start, the rig image and RunPod. The other boxes are the owner's repository settings.

